+        // Plume creates every buffer and image VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE and
+        // never emits a queue family ownership transfer: both ends of each
+        // barrier are VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED. A resource written on one
+        // family therefore has undefined contents on another, and RT64's
+        // texture path does exactly that - TMEM is uploaded on the copy queue,
+        // then read by the decode compute shader on the direct queue with only
+        // a semaphore between them, which orders execution but transfers no
+        // ownership. GPUs that expose a single combined family are unaffected
+        // because every pick resolves to the same index. Imagination's PowerVR
+        // exposes separate families, so keep the virtual queues on the direct
+        // family until plume implements real ownership transfers.
+        if (physicalDeviceProperties.vendorID == 0x1010) {
